  "intro": "Daniel and Layla are flying from Cairo to Amman to visit their friend Yusuf, who is back home in Jordan. At the airport you need one polite question more than any other: هَلْ مِنَ الْمُمْكِن أَنْ…؟ (is it possible to…?). After أَنْ comes a verb that shows the person and ends in -a: هَلْ مِنَ الْمُمْكِن أَنْ أَجْلِسَ بِجَانِبِ النَّافِذَة؟ (could I sit by the window?). The friendly answer is نَعَم، مُمْكِن (yes, that's possible).",
